<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<div xmlns:eac="http://archivists.org/ns/eac/v2" xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:ead="https://archivists.org/ns/ead/v4" type="elementDocumentation" xml:id="elem-legalStatus">
               <head>
                  <gi>legalStatus</gi>
               </head>
               <div type="fullName">
                  <p>Legal Status</p>
               </div>
               <div type="summary">
                  <p type="eac">A required child element of <gi>legalStatuses</gi> used to encode information about the legal status of a corporate body.</p>
                 <p type="ead">An element for indicating the statutorily defined status of the materials being described.</p>
               </div>
               <div type="mayContain">
                  <p><list type="gloss">
  <label>date or dateRange or dateSet</label>
  <item>0..1</item>
  <label>descriptiveNote</label>
  <item>0..1</item>
  <label>placeName</label>
  <item>0..n</item>
  <label>term</label>
  <item>1..n</item>
</list></p>
               </div>
               <div type="mayOccurWithin">
                  <p type="eac">legalStatuses</p>
                  <p type="ead">identificationData</p>
               </div>
               <div type="attributes">
                  <p>
                     <list type="gloss">
                        <label>audience</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>conventionDeclarationReference</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>id</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>languageOfElement</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>localType</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>localTypeDeclarationReference</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>maintenanceEventReference</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>scriptOfElement</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>sourceReference</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>target</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>valueURI</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>vocabularySource</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                        <label>vocabularySourceURI</label>
                        <item>Optional</item>
                     </list>
                  </p>
               </div>
               <div type="description">
                  <p>The legal status is typically defined and granted by authorities or through authorized agencies. Enter terms in accordance with provisions of the controlling legislation. Terms may be drawn from controlled vocabularies or may be natural language terms.</p>
                  <p><gi>legalStatus</gi> must include at least one <gi>term</gi> element, where the legal status is encoded. <gi>term</gi> can be repeated within <gi>legalStatus</gi> to include translations of the same term. Use the <att>languageOfElement</att> attribute to identify the language used in each <gi>term</gi>.</p>
                  <p>Associated date(s) (<gi>date</gi>, <gi>dateRange</gi>, or <gi>dateSet</gi>) and place(s) (<gi>placeName</gi>) may be included to further constrain the term's meaning. A <gi>descriptiveNote</gi> element may be included if a fuller textual explanation is needed.</p>
                  <p type="eac">Multiple <gi>legalStatus</gi> elements may be grouped within a <gi>legalStatuses</gi> element.</p>
                  <p>The prescribed order of all child elements (both required and optional) is:</p>
                  <list type="simple">
                     <item><gi>term</gi></item>
                     <item>One of <gi>date</gi>, <gi>dateRange</gi>, or <gi>dateSet</gi></item>
                     <item><gi>placeName</gi></item>
                     <item><gi>descriptiveNote</gi></item>
                  </list>
               </div>
               <div type="availability">
                  <p type="eac">Required, repeatable</p>
                  <p type="ead">Optional, repeatable</p>
               </div>
               <div type="examples">
                  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" type="ead"><![CDATA[<legalStatus>
			  <term>Public Record(s)</term>
		  </legalStatus>]]>
		  </egXML>
		       <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" type="ead"><![CDATA[<identificationData>
			       <legalStatus>
			       <term>Student records</term>
			       <descriptiveNote>
			       <p>Student records are governed by the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), 20 U.S.C. § 1232g.</p>
		       </descriptiveNote>
		       </legalStatus>
			       <legalStatus>
			       <term>Patient records</term>
			       <descriptiveNote>
			       <p>Patient records are governed by the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act, Pub.L. 104–191 and 110 Stat. 1936. Article 8 ECHR may also apply.</p>
		       </descriptiveNote>
		       </legalStatus>
		       </identificationData>]]>
		       </egXML
		  <egXML xml:lang="eng" type="eac"><![CDATA[<legalStatus>
			  <term>Department of State</term>
		  </legalStatus>]]></egXML>
                  <egXML xml:lang="eng" type="eac"><![CDATA[<legalStatus>
			  <term>Organismo de la Administracion Central del Estado</term>
			  <date standardDate="1769">1769</date>
		  </legalStatus>]]></egXML>
               </div>
            </div>
